#: ../../../converters.md:34
msgid "Writing Formulas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../converters.md:36
msgid ""
"Assignments to {attr}`Range.formula <xlwings.Range.formula>` and {attr}"
"`Range.formula2 <xlwings.Range.formula2>` use the same converters, options, "
"and shape handling as {attr}`Range.value <xlwings.Range.value>` on all "
"engines. Excel turns strings starting with `=` into formulas and writes the "
"other entries as values. Scalars fill the target range, flat lists write a "
"row by default, and two-dimensional data determines the written range's "
"size. Use `myrange.options(transpose=True).formula = formulas` to write a "
"flat list vertically. With the default converter, `None` clears a cell, and "
"dates are written as dates. This doesn't change formula reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../converters.md:38
msgid ""
"A scalar formula such as `myrange.formula = \"=A1*2\"` fills the whole "
"target range, and Excel adjusts its relative references for each cell. In a "
"list, each formula is written exactly as given."
msgstr ""

